From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeebshihadeh@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:41:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] comma: support the mainline kernel's display and touchscreen

The COMMA backend was written for the downstream kernel, whose display
path is ION buffers turned by the SDE rotator. Mainline msm DRM has
neither, and its DPU can't rotate by 90 degrees on SDM845:

- Turn rlsw's landscape target into the portrait panel on the CPU, into
  one of two dumb buffers, in square tiles so the reads stay in cache
  and the write-combined panel buffer is written a row at a time.
- Present each frame with a blocking atomic commit that changes only the
  primary plane's FB_ID, and modeset (drmModeSetCrtc) only when the CRTC
  isn't showing a framebuffer. The commit returns once the frame is
  latched at vblank, which paces the UI to the panel and frees the
  previous buffer. magic hands every client the same DRM file, so a
  client can't count on reading its own flip events, and a flip queued
  before the last one completes fails with EBUSY; a blocking commit
  needs neither. A modeset per frame would include the connector, whose
  encoder->crtc link msm clears and restores in every such commit while
  DPU reads it from the vblank IRQ ("no encoder found for crtc 0").
- Find the backlight under /sys/class/backlight instead of assuming the
  downstream panel0-backlight name.
- Take the panel orientation from the devicetree model, since there's no
  som_id, before and independently of the touchscreen.
- Open the touchscreen by its stable by-path name, seed each slot's
  position from the kernel (evdev only reports changed axes), and track
  the active slot per device. Run without touch rather than exit if it
  is missing.
